    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Owners can now be created with an optional `title` (MR, MRS, MS or DR), and responses include `salutation`: the title, a space and the last name, or just the last name when there's no title. The full test suite passes (17 tests, 0 failures), including the new acceptance test that expects `\"DR who\"`.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **API spec (`openapi.yml`):** added `title` to the owner request fields, limited to MR, MRS, MS and DR, and added a read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` response. Any other title value gets a 400.\n- **Storage:** added a `title` column to the `owners` table in the h2, hsqldb, mysql and postgres schemas, and a matching `title` field on the `Owner` entity. The JDBC repository's select and update statements now include it too.\n- **`OwnerMapper`:** builds `salutation` from the title and last name.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.updateOwner`:** an update replaces the title. Unlike birth date, leaving it out of a PUT clears the title rather than keeping the old one.\n\nThere's no test for the no-title case (salutation is just the last name). It's a one-line branch, but I can add a test for it if you want.",
